      {
        "type": "GeneralText",
        "content": "<h2>About&nbsp;the&nbsp;Major&nbsp;in&nbsp;East&nbsp;Asian&nbsp;Religion,&nbsp;Thought,&nbsp;and&nbsp;Culture</h2><p>For&nbsp;nearly&nbsp;150&nbsp;years,&nbsp;the&nbsp;Department&nbsp;of&nbsp;East&nbsp;Asian&nbsp;Languages&nbsp;and&nbsp;Cultures&nbsp;(EALC)&nbsp;has&nbsp;been&nbsp;the&nbsp;academic&nbsp;center&nbsp;for&nbsp;East&nbsp;Asian&nbsp;Humanities&nbsp;at&nbsp;UC&nbsp;Berkeley.&nbsp;</p><p>The&nbsp;major&nbsp;in&nbsp;East&nbsp;Asian&nbsp;Religion,&nbsp;Thought,&nbsp;and&nbsp;Culture&nbsp;invites&nbsp;you&nbsp;to&nbsp;explore&nbsp;the&nbsp;diverse&nbsp;philosophical&nbsp;and&nbsp;religious&nbsp;traditions&nbsp;of&nbsp;East&nbsp;Asia.&nbsp;This&nbsp;interdisciplinary&nbsp;program&nbsp;trains&nbsp;you&nbsp;to&nbsp;understand&nbsp;these&nbsp;traditions&nbsp;through&nbsp;a&nbsp;deep&nbsp;familiarity&nbsp;with&nbsp;the&nbsp;texts,&nbsp;languages,&nbsp;and&nbsp;cultures&nbsp;that&nbsp;shaped&nbsp;them.</p><p></p><p>Your&nbsp;coursework&nbsp;will&nbsp;combine&nbsp;language&nbsp;acquisition&nbsp;in&nbsp;introductory&nbsp;and&nbsp;intermediate&nbsp;Chinese,&nbsp;Japanese,&nbsp;or&nbsp;Tibetan&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;comparative&nbsp;study&nbsp;of&nbsp;East&nbsp;Asian&nbsp;societies.&nbsp;Learning&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;these&nbsp;languages&nbsp;allows&nbsp;you&nbsp;to&nbsp;access&nbsp;foundational&nbsp;texts&nbsp;directly,&nbsp;without&nbsp;relying&nbsp;on&nbsp;translation.&nbsp;You&nbsp;will&nbsp;broaden&nbsp;your&nbsp;perspective&nbsp;by&nbsp;taking&nbsp;core&nbsp;subjects&nbsp;in&nbsp;Buddhist,&nbsp;Chinese,&nbsp;Japanese,&nbsp;or&nbsp;Tibetan&nbsp;traditions,&nbsp;alongside&nbsp;disciplinary&nbsp;breadth&nbsp;courses&nbsp;in&nbsp;areas&nbsp;like&nbsp;Art&nbsp;History,&nbsp;Film,&nbsp;History,&nbsp;Music,&nbsp;Philosophy,&nbsp;and&nbsp;Religious&nbsp;Studies.&nbsp;Additionally,&nbsp;a&nbsp;dedicated&nbsp;tools&nbsp;and&nbsp;methods&nbsp;course&nbsp;ensures&nbsp;you&nbsp;cultivate&nbsp;strong&nbsp;research&nbsp;and&nbsp;analytical&nbsp;abilities.</p><p></p><p>Students&nbsp;in&nbsp;this&nbsp;major&nbsp;join&nbsp;a&nbsp;vibrant&nbsp;and&nbsp;inclusive&nbsp;academic&nbsp;community,&nbsp;with&nbsp;opportunities&nbsp;to&nbsp;connect&nbsp;and&nbsp;share&nbsp;research&nbsp;through&nbsp;departmental&nbsp;events&nbsp;like&nbsp;our&nbsp;EALC&nbsp;Talks!&nbsp;series.&nbsp;The&nbsp;rigorous&nbsp;interdisciplinary&nbsp;training,&nbsp;effective&nbsp;writing,&nbsp;and&nbsp;critical&nbsp;thinking&nbsp;skills&nbsp;you&nbsp;develop&nbsp;here&nbsp;provide&nbsp;a&nbsp;powerful&nbsp;foundation&nbsp;for&nbsp;advanced&nbsp;studies&nbsp;and&nbsp;diverse&nbsp;professional&nbsp;paths,&nbsp;including&nbsp;law,&nbsp;business,&nbsp;education,&nbsp;and&nbsp;Asian&nbsp;Studies.</p><p></p><h2>Direct&nbsp;Admission&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;Major</h2><p>When&nbsp;you&nbsp;are&nbsp;admitted&nbsp;to&nbsp;UC&nbsp;Berkeley&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;Major&nbsp;in&nbsp;East&nbsp;Asian&nbsp;Religion&nbsp;Thought&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Culture,&nbsp;you&nbsp;enter&nbsp;directly&nbsp;into&nbsp;the&nbsp;major.&nbsp;There&nbsp;is&nbsp;no&nbsp;secondary&nbsp;application&nbsp;or&nbsp;declaration&nbsp;process&nbsp;after&nbsp;you&nbsp;arrive&nbsp;on&nbsp;campus.&nbsp;</p><p>You&nbsp;are&nbsp;a&nbsp;full&nbsp;member&nbsp;of&nbsp;our&nbsp;department&nbsp;from&nbsp;day&nbsp;one.</p><p></p><p>While&nbsp;it&nbsp;is&nbsp;possible&nbsp;to&nbsp;change&nbsp;your&nbsp;major&nbsp;after&nbsp;you&nbsp;matriculate&nbsp;to&nbsp;Berkeley,&nbsp;switching&nbsp;into&nbsp;a&nbsp;high-demand&nbsp;field&nbsp;like&nbsp;Business,&nbsp;Computer&nbsp;Science,&nbsp;Economics,&nbsp;or&nbsp;Psychology&nbsp;may&nbsp;require&nbsp;you&nbsp;to&nbsp;pass&nbsp;a&nbsp;competitive&nbsp;comprehensive&nbsp;review&nbsp;process.&nbsp;Additionally,&nbsp;spending&nbsp;your&nbsp;time&nbsp;preparing&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;different&nbsp;program&nbsp;once&nbsp;you&nbsp;arrive&nbsp;on&nbsp;campus&nbsp;will&nbsp;cause&nbsp;a&nbsp;lack&nbsp;of&nbsp;progress&nbsp;in&nbsp;your&nbsp;currently&nbsp;declared&nbsp;major,&nbsp;which&nbsp;can&nbsp;delay&nbsp;your&nbsp;graduation.&nbsp;</p><p>We&nbsp;want&nbsp;to&nbsp;ensure&nbsp;you&nbsp;choose&nbsp;the&nbsp;path&nbsp;that&nbsp;best&nbsp;supports&nbsp;your&nbsp;long-term&nbsp;goals&nbsp;and&nbsp;allows&nbsp;you&nbsp;to&nbsp;graduate&nbsp;on&nbsp;time.</p><p></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Personal&nbsp;Advising&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Your&nbsp;Transition</strong></p><p>To&nbsp;support&nbsp;a&nbsp;smooth&nbsp;transition,&nbsp;all&nbsp;admitted&nbsp;transfer&nbsp;students&nbsp;are&nbsp;required&nbsp;to&nbsp;meet&nbsp;with&nbsp;our&nbsp;undergraduate&nbsp;advisor&nbsp;before&nbsp;enrolling&nbsp;in&nbsp;their&nbsp;first&nbsp;semester&nbsp;of&nbsp;classes.&nbsp;</p><p>This&nbsp;is&nbsp;our&nbsp;way&nbsp;of&nbsp;welcoming&nbsp;you&nbsp;and&nbsp;ensuring&nbsp;your&nbsp;academic&nbsp;plan&nbsp;matches&nbsp;your&nbsp;interests&nbsp;and&nbsp;graduation&nbsp;goals.</p><p>You&nbsp;will&nbsp;receive&nbsp;detailed&nbsp;instructions&nbsp;on&nbsp;how&nbsp;to&nbsp;schedule&nbsp;this&nbsp;meeting&nbsp;well&nbsp;before&nbsp;your&nbsp;first&nbsp;semester&nbsp;begins,&nbsp;either&nbsp;through&nbsp;the&nbsp;summer&nbsp;Golden&nbsp;Bear&nbsp;Advising&nbsp;program&nbsp;or&nbsp;via&nbsp;a&nbsp;direct&nbsp;email&nbsp;from&nbsp;our&nbsp;department.&nbsp;</p><p>We&nbsp;look&nbsp;forward&nbsp;to&nbsp;meeting&nbsp;you&nbsp;and&nbsp;helping&nbsp;you&nbsp;plan&nbsp;your&nbsp;time&nbsp;at&nbsp;Berkeley.</p><p></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">PREPARATION&nbsp;FOR&nbsp;THE&nbsp;MAJOR&nbsp;IN&nbsp;EAST&nbsp;ASIAN&nbsp;RELIGION&nbsp;THOUGHT&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;CULTURE</strong></p><p></p><p>Courses&nbsp;related&nbsp;to&nbsp;East&nbsp;Asian&nbsp;philosophy,&nbsp;religion,&nbsp;and&nbsp;culture&nbsp;are&nbsp;recommended&nbsp;and&nbsp;may&nbsp;be&nbsp;transferable&nbsp;for&nbsp;credit&nbsp;toward&nbsp;major&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;upon&nbsp;consultation&nbsp;with&nbsp;the&nbsp;undergraduate&nbsp;major&nbsp;advisor&nbsp;(UMA).</p><p></p><p>We&nbsp;encourage&nbsp;Students&nbsp;to&nbsp;take&nbsp;Chinese,&nbsp;Japanese,&nbsp;or&nbsp;Tibetan&nbsp;language&nbsp;courses&nbsp;if&nbsp;they&nbsp;are&nbsp;offered&nbsp;at&nbsp;their&nbsp;college.&nbsp;Students&nbsp;will&nbsp;receive&nbsp;transfer&nbsp;credit&nbsp;for&nbsp;language&nbsp;courses&nbsp;taken&nbsp;at&nbsp;their&nbsp;community&nbsp;college.&nbsp;However,&nbsp;all&nbsp;UC&nbsp;Berkeley&nbsp;students&nbsp;must&nbsp;take&nbsp;a<a href=\"https://ealc.berkeley.edu/programs/undergraduate/placement-exams\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">&nbsp;placement&nbsp;exam&nbsp;for&nbsp;Chinese&nbsp;or&nbsp;Japanese</a>&nbsp;(there&nbsp;are&nbsp;no&nbsp;placement&nbsp;exams&nbsp;for&nbsp;Tibetan)&nbsp;to&nbsp;ensure&nbsp;enrollment&nbsp;in&nbsp;a&nbsp;course&nbsp;at&nbsp;the&nbsp;correct&nbsp;level&nbsp;for&nbsp;their&nbsp;language&nbsp;skills.&nbsp;Because&nbsp;language&nbsp;courses&nbsp;vary&nbsp;across&nbsp;colleges,&nbsp;a&nbsp;student&nbsp;may&nbsp;need&nbsp;to&nbsp;repeat&nbsp;an&nbsp;introductory&nbsp;or&nbsp;intermediate-level&nbsp;course.&nbsp;The&nbsp;department&nbsp;undergraduate&nbsp;advisor&nbsp;will&nbsp;work&nbsp;with&nbsp;students&nbsp;to&nbsp;create&nbsp;a&nbsp;program&nbsp;plan&nbsp;to&nbsp;complete&nbsp;their&nbsp;major&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;by&nbsp;their&nbsp;expected&nbsp;graduation&nbsp;date,&nbsp;regardless&nbsp;of&nbsp;which&nbsp;language&nbsp;course&nbsp;is&nbsp;their&nbsp;first.&nbsp;</p><p></p><p>Please&nbsp;note:&nbsp;Advanced&nbsp;Placement&nbsp;(AP)&nbsp;and&nbsp;International&nbsp;Baccalaureate&nbsp;(IB)&nbsp;exams&nbsp;will&nbsp;not&nbsp;satisfy&nbsp;the&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;this&nbsp;major.</p><p></p><p><strong>More&nbsp;Information</strong></p><p>The&nbsp;<a href=\"https://undergraduate.catalog.berkeley.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Berkeley&nbsp;Catalog</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://ealc.berkeley.edu/programs/undergraduate/undergraduate-requirements/east-asian-religion-major-requirements\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">department&nbsp;website</a>&nbsp;provide&nbsp;more&nbsp;information&nbsp;about&nbsp;major&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;and&nbsp;course&nbsp;information.</p><p></p><p><strong>Advising:</strong></p><p>Students&nbsp;with&nbsp;questions&nbsp;about&nbsp;transferring&nbsp;into&nbsp;the&nbsp;major&nbsp;in&nbsp;East&nbsp;Asian&nbsp;Languages&nbsp;and&nbsp;Cultures&nbsp;are&nbsp;encouraged&nbsp;to&nbsp;contact&nbsp;our&nbsp;undergraduate&nbsp;major&nbsp;advisor:</p><p>Cassandra&nbsp;Dunn</p><p>Department&nbsp;Website:&nbsp;<a href=\"http://ealc.berkeley.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">http://ealc.berkeley.edu/</a></p><p>Email:&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:cassandrajj@berkeley.edu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">cassandrajj@berkeley.edu</a></p><p>Appointments:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://calendly.com/cassandra-dunn-ug-advisor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Schedule&nbsp;an&nbsp;appointment&nbsp;(in-person&nbsp;or&nbsp;remotely).</a></p>",
        "groupId": "47e56f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
